<title>LEBANON: Lebanon public debt up 2.51 pct in Apr-May.</title>
<headline>Lebanon public debt up 2.51 pct in Apr-May.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's public debt rose by 2.51 percent in May over April according to figures issued by the Lebanese Banks Association on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It rose 12.5 percent to 22,622 billion pounds from 20,109 billion pounds at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>The cumulative deficit of income to expenditure fell to 56.3 percent from 60.3 percent in April. It was 51.5 percent at the end of December 1996, the association said.</p>
<p>The association issued the following details of Lebanon's public finances (billions of Lebanese pounds at end of period unless otherwise stated):</p>
<p>			    May 97   Apr 97   Mar 97    Dec 96/May 97</p>
<p>Revenues</p>
<p>(Cumulative)	     1,404     954	  719</p>
<p>monthly change	     450     235	  204</p>
<p>Expenses (Cumulative)  3,216   2,404	1,785</p>
<p>Monthly change	     812     619	  704</p>
<p>Deficit (Cumulative)   1,812   1,450	1,066</p>
<p>Monthly change	     362     384	  500</p>
<p>Deficit/ expenses	 56.3%   60.3%	59.7%     9.33%</p>
<p>Total debt		  22,622  22,068     21,711   12.50%</p>
<p>Monthly change	     2.51    1.64	 2.30</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057  745307  745308</p>
